  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_019 (scvi_n200, vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.706 accuracy, dramatically outperforming all scgpt-based configs (~0.52-0.54), establishing scvi_n200 as the dominant RNA encoder. Within scgpt configs, weighted fusion > concat (0.542 vs 0.518) and vit_l > resnet50 (0.542 vs 0.525). The only untested dimension with the best-known components is aggregation: all top configs used avgpool. Question: Does transformer aggregation improve upon avgpool when paired with the strong scvi_n200 + vit_l + weighted combination? This is the most informative exploitation step because it tests whether the remaining architectural lever (aggregation) can push accuracy beyond 0.706. If transformer helps, it opens a new high-performing family; if not, we confirm avgpool is sufficient and can focus remaining budget on singleprofile or other refinements. Expected cost: transformer aggregation adds self-attention over profiles, so I estimate ~5-7 GPU hours (moderately above config_019's 4.82), keeping total budget well within reasonable bounds with 5 experiments remaining."
}

